This repository contains several kinds of original work and therefore uses a mixed-license policy.

## 1. Software and formal-proof source — MIT

Unless a file states otherwise, original source code and machine-executable material in this repository — including Lean source, Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, shell/batch scripts, build tools, CI/workflow code, and reusable software modules — is licensed under the MIT License.

See `LICENSES/MIT.txt`.

## 2. Scholarly content — CC BY 4.0

Unless a file states otherwise, original scholarly prose, research notes, documentation, tables, diagrams, figures, and original research datasets owned by Jeromie N. Beasley are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license (CC BY 4.0).

CC BY 4.0 permits sharing and adaptation, including commercial use, subject to its attribution requirements. Appropriate credit should identify Jeromie N. Beasley as creator, identify the source work/repository when practical, link the license, and indicate modifications when required by the license.

License deed and legal code:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

See `LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.md`.

## 3. Third-party material

Third-party papers, quoted material, datasets, figures, software, and other imported sources are NOT relicensed by this notice. They remain governed by their original copyright, license, citation, database, or use terms. Attribution records in the research files should be preserved.

## 4. File-specific terms control

A license or rights statement attached to an individual file, dataset, paper, archive, subdirectory, or imported source overrides this repository-level default for that material.

## 5. Prior CC0 publication history

Before 10 September 2026, the repository root exposed a CC0 1.0 Universal notice. CC0 is designed as an irrevocable public-domain dedication/license fallback. This licensing change does not attempt to withdraw rights already granted for versions or material that were publicly released under CC0.

The MIT / CC BY 4.0 policy above applies to new original contributions and newly published versions from the commit introducing this notice forward, subject to any rights already granted under CC0 and to any file-specific or third-party terms.

## 6. Citation and scientific priority

Licensing permission and scientific attribution are separate questions. When using research results, proofs, figures, datasets, or substantial software from this repository, please cite the relevant paper/release/DOI when available and preserve the author and provenance information.

The repository-level citation record is in `CITATION.cff`.
